# HOSSPI HMS App Write-Up

HOSSPI HMS means HOSSPI Hospital Management System.

## Core Modules

| Module | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| App shell | Brand the app and host navigation, badges, and status. |
| Auth/session | Handle login, logout, sessions, and route guards. |
| General settings | Store user preferences and accessibility defaults. |
| Tenant settings | Manage tenant profile, settings, and enabled modules. |
| Facility settings | Manage facility profile, structure, and service points. |
| Users/roles/permissions | Manage staff accounts, roles, and access scope. |
| Subscriptions | Manage plans, entitlements, invoices, and renewal state. |
| Rooms/wards/beds | Manage care spaces, occupancy, and assignments. |
| Patient registry | Register patients and maintain lookup data. |
| OPD flow | Manage arrivals, queues, routing, and completion. |
| Triage | Capture vitals, complaints, and routing decisions. |
| Clinical | Manage encounters, notes, orders, and follow-up. |
| Nursing | Manage tasks, medication administration, and handover. |
| IPD | Manage admissions, beds, rounds, and transfers. |
| ICU | Manage critical-care stays, monitoring, and readiness. |
| Theater | Manage bookings, procedures, anesthesia, and handover. |
| Discharge | Complete discharge checks, summaries, and closure. |
| Emergency/ambulance | Manage emergency intake, dispatch, and handoff. |
| Laboratory | Manage samples, results, and quality checks. |
| Radiology | Manage imaging orders, studies, and results. |
| Physiotherapy | Manage therapy plans, sessions, and progress. |
| Pharmacy | Manage formularies, dispensing, stock, and returns. |
| Billing/cashier | Manage invoices, payments, refunds, and closeout. |
| Insurance/claims | Manage coverage, claims, and claim tracking. |
| HR | Manage staff profiles, shifts, leave, and payroll. |
| Biomedical | Manage equipment, maintenance, and safety work. |
| Operations | Manage non-clinical facility maintenance and readiness. |
| Housekeeping | Manage cleaning, turnover, and sanitation readiness. |
| Mortuary | Manage custody, storage, release, and mortuary events. |
| Notifications | Manage alerts, messages, and badge state. |
| Reports/audit | Manage dashboards, reports, exports, and audit logs. |
| Integrations | Manage keys, webhooks, logs, and external status. |
| Demo seed | Provide safe non-production seed data. |
| Dental | Manage oral care workflows, charting, and follow-up. |

## Module Boundaries

- Tenant and facility settings own structure; other modules must consume it.
- Access modules own account access; other modules must request allowed actions only.
- Patient-care modules must keep their own workflows focused and self-contained.
- Reports and audit must read from modules, not replace them.
- Dental must stay within outpatient and emergency dental care.

## Patient Flow Documents

Use `flows/` when changing workflow behavior.

| Flow | Scope |
|---|---|
| `opd-flow.mdc` | Outpatient queues and handoff |
| `ipd-flow.mdc` | Inpatient admission and stay |
| `emergency-flow.mdc` | Emergency intake and transfer |
| `icu-flow.mdc` | ICU overlay on admission |
| `theater-flow.mdc` | Surgical episode overlay |
| `nursing-flow.mdc` | Ward nursing and vitals |
| `lab-flow.mdc` | Lab order execution |
| `radiology-flow.mdc` | Imaging order execution |
| `pharmacy-flow.mdc` | Dispensing and discharge meds |
| `discharge-flow.mdc` | IPD discharge clearance |

## Demo Seeds

- Demo data must be clearly marked, safe to reset, and never required in production.

